erence between different workload types\n\n## When to use each\n\n| Mode | Best for |\n|------|----------|\n| **1** | General use, default, best compatibility |\n| **2** | Compute-heavy workloads wanting dedicated CCS slots |\n| **4** | Workloads needing maximum isolation between context types |\n\n---\n\n**Important caveat:** I'm not fully certain about the exact semantics of mode 4 versus mode 2, and the Xe driver's CCS mode behavior has evolved across kernel versions. The precise definitions can vary depending on your kernel version.\n\nFor accurate, version-specific details, I'd recommend checking:\n- The kernel source: `drivers/gpu/drm/xe/` (look for `ccs_mode` definitions)\n- The `Documentation/` files in your kernel tree\n- `dmesg` output showing which mode was selected at boot\n\nWould you like me to help you find"}